  "_fixture_note": [
    "`terraform show -json` output, deliberately awkward — the shape",
    "awkward.tfstate.json cannot express, because the two formats disagree about",
    "how they say the same things.",
    "",
    "Verified against terraform's own marshaller on main (2026-08-08):",
    "  internal/command/jsonstate/state.go",
    "    Resource.DeposedKey  `json:\"deposed_key,omitempty\"`   (line ~114)",
    "    Resource.Tainted     `json:\"tainted,omitempty\"`       (line ~111)",
    "    marshalResources     lines ~481-529: every deposed object is emitted as",
    "                         a SEPARATE Resource entry whose Address is",
    "                         `current.Address` — byte for byte the same address",
    "                         as the live object — with DeposedKey set.",
    "",
    "So a state mid-replace yields two entries at one address here, where raw v4",
    "yields two `instances[]` under one resource. A parser that only knows the v4",
    "spelling emits two `import` blocks for one address: invalid HCL, and the",
    "second one adopts the object terraform is about to destroy.",
    "",
    "Note also that jsonstate carries NO provider alias — ProviderName is the",
    "provider *source address* (registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/aws), not the",
    "config address — so cross-account provenance is only recoverable from raw",
    "v4. See two-account.tfstate.json for that half."
  ],
